   "section_y": -1,
   "indent": 0,
   "parent": null,
   "text": "1If SBP < 80, pulse ≥ 100, respiratory rate > 30, confusion/restlessness, weakness, shock likely. 2Black stools may be caused by iron tablets. Only refer if black stools started before iron treatment. 3Mean cell volume (MCV) helps identify cause of anaemia. Check on FBC result sheet if MCV low, normal or high compared to reference range. 4Drinks > 14 drinks/week or ≥ 4 drinks/session. One drink is 1 tot of spirits, or 1 small glass (125mL) of wine or 1 can/bottle (330mL) of beer.",
   "bbox": [
